# Round trips to the Git host, per operation.
# Generated by TestGitRoundTripLedger; specified by
# docs/design/push-notification-and-reconcile-trigger.md §1.6.
#
# Regenerate with:  go test ./internal/git -run TestGitRoundTripLedger -update
#
# conn is the total number of requests to the Git host, which is the cost this
# design optimizes. Each request column reads  <count> <request>/<response>,
# where the two sizes are classes rather than byte counts: a packfile is
# compressed content carrying timestamps and hashes, so its exact length is not
# reproducible, while "did this conversation move a tree" is. Run the test with
# -v for the exact bytes.
#
# fetch-open = GET /info/refs?service=git-upload-pack   (a fetch conversation)
# fetch-xfer = POST /git-upload-pack                    (objects requested)
# push-open  = GET /info/refs?service=git-receive-pack  (the CAS advertisement)
# push-xfer  = POST /git-receive-pack                   (a packfile sent)

operation                                                   conn  fetch-open    fetch-xfer    push-open     push-xfer   
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. bootstrap helper, empty remote                              1  1 -/<1K       0             0             0           
2. bootstrap helper, populated remote                          3  2 -/<1K       1 <1K/<1K     0             0           
3. one publication, one commit                                 2  0             0             1 -/<1K       1 <1K/<1K   
4. one publication, several commits in one cycle               2  0             0             1 -/<1K       1 <4K/<1K   
5. a publication that commits nothing                          1  0             0             1 -/<1K       0           
6. a publication whose push is rejected once, then succeeds     6  2 -/<1K       1 <1K/<4K     2 -/<1K       1 <1K/<1K   
7. a publication rejected twice                               10  4 -/<4K       2 <1K/<4K     3 -/<1K       1 <1K/<1K   
8. forced recheck, no retained writes                          2  2 -/<1K       0             0             0           
9. forced recheck, with retained writes                        2  2 -/<1K       0             0             0           
10. a resync (snapshot)                                        4  2 -/<1K       0             1 -/<1K       1 <1K/<1K   
11. an idle target held across several commit windows          0  0             0             0             0           
